<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  com.scannerproject.wx-decoder-watchdog

  Guarantees the box is never left with no weather/ACARS decoder.

  The RSPduo (180903EF32) serves either ACARS+VDL2 (acarsdec mode=MA +
  dumpvdl2 mode=SL tuner=2) or radiosonde (auto_rx, mode=ST) – never both –
  so /api/wx/decoder hands it over by booting one side out and starting the
  other.

  The hazard: com.scannerproject.radiosonde ships RunAtLoad=false AND
  KeepAlive=false, so if auto_rx dies nothing restarts it, and ACARS does not
  return either – the handoff booted it out of the launchd domain, which is
  exactly what prevents its own KeepAlive from recovering it. A crash at 3am
  used to mean no ACARS, no radiosonde, and no sign anything had happened.

  This runs every 60 s and:
    * does nothing while the requested decoder is actually running;
    * retries radiosonde up to 3 consecutive times if that is what was asked
      for, so a transient failure does not silently end an overnight session;
    * restores ACARS (the KeepAlive=true baseline) once that budget is spent.

  It reads the requested decoder from ~/.local/share/sb3/wx_decoder_intent,
  which sb3/ui/routes.py:_wx_decoder_switch writes before it starts work.
  Without that it could not tell a dead radiosonde session from a deliberate
  ACARS one.

  StartInterval rather than KeepAlive: this is a periodic check, not a daemon.
  RunAtLoad so a reboot gets a check immediately rather than 60 s later.

  Install:
    cp etc/mac/launchd/neptune/com.scannerproject.wx-decoder-watchdog.plist \
       ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) \
       ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.scannerproject.wx-decoder-watchdog.plist

  Log: ~/Library/Logs/sb3/wx-decoder-watchdog.log (the script also writes
  there itself, so the launchd stdio files stay small).
-->
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.scannerproject.wx-decoder-watchdog</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/willminkoff/scannerproject/macos/bin/wx-decoder-watchdog.py</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/willminkoff/scannerproject</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/willminkoff/Library/Logs/sb3/wx-decoder-watchdog.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/willminkoff/Library/Logs/sb3/wx-decoder-watchdog.out</string>
</dict>
</plist>
